    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-18T15:55:47+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-18T15:55:47+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T05:25:47Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T05:25:47Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A slow-moving high pressure system over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge over eastern SA. A trough of low pressure over WA will move eastwards into western SA late Sunday and reach southeastern parts later Monday, while a weakening cold front crosses the Bight. The trough lingers in the east through the middle of the week as a weak high pressure system forms in the Bight. This trough weakens on Thursday as a second trough moves into the west from WA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-18T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor, becoming less likely later tonight. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds west of Nullarbor. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. High chance of showers east of Ceduna, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then becoming southerly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 33.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Streaky Bay in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Ceduna in the early morning. Winds southerly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to southeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of morning fog south of Streaky Bay. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northwesterly during the day then shifting south to southeasterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
